  "安全・規制・保管": [
   {
    "quote": "Modern SLA, DLP and MSLA photopolymer resins consist of reactive acrylate monomers and oligomers that polymerize into solid polymers when exposed to <405 nm UV light, triggered by photoinitiators. Before that reaction is complete, these chemicals are hazardous to your skin, lungs and the environment.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "Water-washable SLA resin contains the same hazardous acrylate monomers as standard resin. It just dissolves in water instead of IPA.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "Multiple manufacturers’ own Safety Data Sheets classify their water-washable resins as “Environmentally Hazardous Substance” that is “toxic to aquatic life with long lasting effects.”",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "Safety Data Sheet (SDS",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "Short answer: No, these terms do not mean that the resins do not contain any hazardous components.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "These resins undergo heavy chemical modification and still contain hazardous components.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "Commonly available plant-based resins contain substantial amounts of epoxidized soybean oil oligomer (a skin irritant) alongside standard resin chemicals including isooctyl acrylate (respiratory toxicity), photoinitiators (organ toxicity) and other hazardous compounds.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "The real danger of bio-based resins is not that they are more toxic. It is that the marketing actively misleads users into skipping PPE. Labels like “eco-friendly,” “biodegradable” and “plant-based” signal safety to most people. The SDS tells a different story than the front of the bottle.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "Dispose of bio-based resin waste following hazardous material procedures.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "No. Removing certain hazardous ingredients can reduce specific chemical hazards, but it doesn’t make a resin completely safe. Other ingredients may still cause skin allergies, irritation or other health problems.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "Always check the resin’s Safety Data Sheet (SDS).",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "Use effective ventilation during printing, washing and curing. Follow the SDS and safety guidance for any additional protection needed.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "No. Having a Safety Data Sheet (SDS) doesn’t mean a resin is safe or free from hazardous ingredients. What matters is the information inside it, so don’t just check whether an SDS exists. Read it.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "If a resin manufacturer provides an SDS, the product must be safe and properly tested.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "An SDS is a standardized safety document, so it’s easy to assume that having one means the product has been tested and approved as safe.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   }
  ],
  "品質・証明": [
   {
    "quote": "Do not use: surgical masks, N95/KN95 respirators, dust masks or cloth masks.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "First, printer lids do not seal airtight. VOCs escape through gaps around the lid, the build plate slot, cable pass-throughs and any venting holes in the housing. The leak rate is slow enough that you may not notice the smell, but VOC concentrations in the room still rise throughout a multi-hour print. You are breathing contaminated air for the entire print duration without realizing it.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "And printing is only one part of the whole workflow. There’s also washing, post-curing, and a lot of handling of uncured prints, liquid resin and washing liquids. Often, all of this happens in the same room. Many VOCs are released during these steps, and a printer’s low-emission certification does not automatically mean that these parts of the process have also been evaluated or certified.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "Never use the printing area for food, clothing or children’s items.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "If you must use resin for food applications, coat with an FDA-compliant or EU Regulation 10/2011-compliant food-safe epoxy.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "Consider coating with clear epoxy or polyurethane for skin-contact items.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "Wash your hands and change your clothes before handling children or pets after a print session.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "Disposable aprons or dedicated printing clothes",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "Prevent resin transfer to personal clothing",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   }
  ],
  "装置縛り・オープン材料": [
   {
    "quote": "with appropriate cartridges (such as 3M 6075, 3M 6005) during printing, cleaning and post-processing.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "Another thing to watch for is how manufacturers disclose ingredients. Some SDSs use terms such as “proprietary,” “trade secret” or broad chemical descriptions instead of identifying specific substances.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "If ingredients are listed as proprietary or the safety information is unclear, ask the manufacturer for clarification.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "Some might think that printers with automatic resin dispensing and sealed cartridges can help. While they reduce the contact during refills, they do not remove it completely. You still handle resin when you take out the tank, remove the build platform, take parts off the plate and carry fresh parts to the wash.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "No. Only organic vapor respirators with proper cartridges protect against resin VOC’s.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "Use an organic vapor (OV) respirator with the right cartridges:",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "3M 6001 Organic Vapor Cartridge (effective against methacrylate and similar acrylates).",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "3M 6075 Formaldehyde/Organic Vapor Cartridge.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "3M 6005 Formaldehyde/Organic Vapor Cartridge.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "Only organic vapor respirators with proper cartridges are effective against VOCs released during resin 3D printing. Use appropriate PPE.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "You may see resins marketed as biocompatible based on testing under ISO 10993, the standard series used for the biological evaluation of medical devices. That result is real, but it is narrower than it sounds.",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "If printing continues, maximize all existing controls: dedicated outdoor exhaust ventilation, fresh organic vapor respirator cartridges changed on schedule, full nitrile glove changes every 5 minutes (depends on resin formulation).",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "Type of Respirator Cartridge",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
   {
    "quote": "3M 6001 Organic Vapor Cartridge – protection against certain organic vapors",
    "url": "https://ameralabs.com/blog/resin-safety-myths-3d-printing/",
    "pass": 3
   },
